# Copy to .env.local (already gitignored) to enable optional cloud
# features in development. The app runs fully offline/local-first with
# both of these unset — see supabase/README.md's "Local development"
# section. Neither value below is a secret:
#
# - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is your project's public API endpoint.
# - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is Supabase's publishable/anon key
#   (legacy JWT anon key, or the newer sb_publishable_... key format —
#   either works). It is designed to be shipped in client code and is
#   safe to commit to a screenshot or bug report; it is meaningless
#   without the Row Level Security policies in supabase/migrations/
#   enforcing access.
#
# The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix means Expo inlines these into the JS bundle at
# build time (babel-preset-expo does this automatically) — anything with
# this prefix is public by definition, so NEVER put a secret here.
#
# NEVER put your project's service-role/secret key in this file or in any
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable. The service-role key bypasses Row Level Security
# entirely and must never exist in client code, only on a trusted server
# you control (none exists in this project yet).

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
